The skill and template text in this repository is an original implementation,
written in Traditional Chinese and English, of the "finding your unknowns"
workflow described publicly by Thariq Shihipar (Anthropic) in "A Field Guide
to Claude Fable 5: Finding Your Unknowns". Credit for the techniques and the
"finding your unknowns" framing belongs to the original author.

Parts of the packaging approach (README structure, the one-file guidance
distribution, and several skill mechanisms noted in the commit history) were
inspired by the community repository Neeeophytee/finding-unknowns-skills
(MIT), whose instruction text is its author's own distillation of the same
essays.

